fix EOD flatten recording held trades as flat +0.00R (masked +4R of real P&L)

The 3:55 PM flatten fell back to entry price when it couldn't match the
liquidation fill in Alpaca's order list, so 7 of 8 hold-to-EOD trades during
the 06-15..18 vacation week recorded exit==entry (+0.00R). Verified against real
~15:55 market closes: those trades were actually +5.57R, not +1.51R recorded.

Impact on the paper record (edge-neutral measurement fix, not a strategy change):
  week total  -6.17R -> -2.11R
  win rate    10%    -> 30%   (vs 37% backtest expectation)
  EOD exits   +0.19R -> +0.70R avg (matches backtest: the edge is in the holds)

Fix: exit-price priority is now liquidation fill -> real market close
(getLatestClose) -> entry as last resort. Never records flat when a market
price is available. Backfilled the 8 affected trades via verify-eod.ts --fix.

Adds diagnostics: vacation-audit.ts (per-day + gap detection), verify-eod.ts.

